<h2>Read Before Upgrading</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>With TUN on, the TUN stack chosen in Clash settings now takes precedence over a Profile's <code>tun.stack</code>.</strong> Previously a stack written by the subscription won. If you relied on it, choose the stack in settings instead (the default is gVisor).</li>
<li><strong>A Profile that sets a TUN stack the selected core rejects now fails to apply, with an error naming the value and the supported ones.</strong> For example, <code>tun.stack: mixed</code> or <code>mips</code> under Clash Premium, which would otherwise make the core reject the whole config. This is checked even while TUN is off, because the core parses the key on load. Values Nyanpasu does not know are still passed to the core.</li>
<li><strong>The stack selector only lists the stacks the current core reads</strong>, and is hidden for clash-rs and Meow, which ignore the key. If the saved stack is not supported by the core you switch to, gVisor is used and a warning is written to the log; the saved setting is kept.</li>
<li><strong>Service mode now requires nyanpasu-service 2.0.2.</strong> An installed 2.0.1 service is upgraded once at startup. 2.0.2 fixes a stale pid record that made the service and the app fail on every start (<a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="6057816219" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/libnyanpasu/clash-nyanpasu/issues/6033" data-hovercard-type="issue" data-hovercard-url="/libnyanpasu/clash-nyanpasu/issues/6033/hovercard" href="https://github.com/libnyanpasu/clash-nyanpasu/issues/6033">#6033</a>).</li>
</ul>
<h2>Highlights</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Mips (Mihomo IP Stack)</strong>, mihomo's new user-space TUN stack, can be selected under mihomo and mihomo-alpha, together with its TCP congestion controller (CUBIC, Reno, BBR, BBRv3, or the core default). The controller is remembered when you switch to another stack and back (<a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="6120977493" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/libnyanpasu/clash-nyanpasu/issues/6091" data-hovercard-type="issue" data-hovercard-url="/libnyanpasu/clash-nyanpasu/issues/6091/hovercard" href="https://github.com/libnyanpasu/clash-nyanpasu/issues/6091">#6091</a>).</li>
<li><strong>Startup failures no longer crash the app.</strong> A dialog names the file, the cause and the recovery steps, and can open the containing, backup or log folder. Corrupt local data and an unusable jobs journal are rebuilt instead of blocking startup.</li>
</ul>
